WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.162
<v Examiner>Her own formative questions on this module.

2
00:00:04.162 --> 00:00:04.994
<v Examiner>Four of them.

3
00:00:05.444 --> 00:00:09.500
These are Joan's own questions, from her formative mini exams.

4
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.332
Answer each one before I do.

5
00:00:11.782 --> 00:00:12.040
<v Examiner>One.

6
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.582
<v Examiner>Sione is scared of becoming dependent on his analgesic.

7
00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.481
<v Examiner>Which description is accurate for dependence?

8
00:00:21.931 --> 00:00:25.980
Withdrawal symptoms if a prescribed drug is stopped abruptly.

9
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:26.577
That's B.

10
00:00:26.577 --> 00:00:32.087
Not the craving answer: craving, loss of control and use despite harm is addiction.

11
00:00:32.087 --> 00:00:34.411
She corrected her own key in class.

12
00:00:34.861 --> 00:00:35.077
<v Examiner>Two.

13
00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:37.293
<v Examiner>What is the definition of drug addiction?

14
00:00:40.743 --> 00:00:42.907
A behavioural pattern of drug use,

15
00:00:42.907 --> 00:00:48.445
where the person experiences overwhelming involvement in getting the drug and using the

16
00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:48.763
drug.

17
00:00:48.763 --> 00:00:51.501
Not decreasing effects with repeated doses.

18
00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:52.583
That's tolerance.

19
00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:53.364
<v Examiner>Three.

20
00:00:53.364 --> 00:00:56.681
<v Examiner>Which statement is the most accurate about controlled drugs?

21
00:01:00.131 --> 00:01:04.496
Controlled drugs are substances subject to special legal controls,

22
00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:06.282
to reduce misuse and abuse.

23
00:01:06.282 --> 00:01:10.052
Not: they're illicit, so they can't be given to patients.

24
00:01:10.052 --> 00:01:13.293
Morphine is controlled, and it's given every day.

25
00:01:13.743 --> 00:01:14.070
<v Examiner>Four.

26
00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.184
<v Examiner>The nurse gave Trevor half a dose of his antibiotic by mistake.

27
00:01:18.184 --> 00:01:20.143
<v Examiner>Which step is not appropriate?

28
00:01:23.593 --> 00:01:25.652
Calling oh eight hundred poison.

29
00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.582
A half dose isn't a poisoning.

30
00:01:27.582 --> 00:01:31.828
Document it, complete an incident report, and tell the prescriber.

31
00:01:32.278 --> 00:01:33.537
<v Examiner>Once more, all four.

32
00:01:35.987 --> 00:01:40.809
Dependence is withdrawal symptoms if a prescribed drug is stopped abruptly,

33
00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:42.160
her corrected key, B.

34
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.410
Addiction is a behavioural pattern,

35
00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:48.268
with overwhelming involvement in getting and using the drug.

36
00:01:48.268 --> 00:01:53.219
Controlled drugs are under special legal controls to reduce misuse and abuse,

37
00:01:53.219 --> 00:01:54.955
and they can be prescribed.

38
00:01:54.955 --> 00:02:00.678
And a half dose given by mistake is a medication error, not a call to the Poisons Centre.
